  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following is not correct for relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> on the set of real numbers?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "GCFma",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is reflexive but not symmetric.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0bGCS",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is reflexive and symmetric.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cFDwS",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is symmetric and transitive.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "XQDuV",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is not transitive but symmetric.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>symmetric</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>transitive<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>is symmetric</p><p>let&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;.......(1)<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> satisfy the equation (1)<br />but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8713;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> not satisfied<br />Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is symmetric but not transitive relation</p>",
